t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(T>{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ and $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1$ degrees of freedom. \n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=35.5,\\,n=25,\\,s=3.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $95%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.95=0.05\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>2.064)=0.025.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}={t}_{24,0.025}=2.064.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}35.5 & \\pm 2.064\\cdot \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\ 35.5 & \\pm 1.238\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a3ddbbb-774a-5798-bdcc-84bb9aeba43b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a3ddbbb-774a-5798-bdcc-84bb9aeba43b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a3ddbbb-774a-5798-bdcc-84bb9aeba43b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4de9d1fa-2114-5200-ac1f-74384ab0d808" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c062760-ad33-5060-805b-7922362c6616" "answer-ca73b624-1cba-5a83-b12e-199698b3233b" "answer-4de9d1fa-2114-5200-ac1f-74384ab0d808" "answer-5af67d73-630d-5855-be78-1f49db4aac29" "answer-b29529d2-fe42-5676-82dd-5a515d0e03fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c062760-ad33-5060-805b-7922362c6616" :answer/id #uuid "3c062760-ad33-5060-805b-7922362c6616" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.5\\pm 0.124" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca73b624-1cba-5a83-b12e-199698b3233b" :answer/id #uuid "ca73b624-1cba-5a83-b12e-199698b3233b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\pm 6.322" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4de9d1fa-2114-5200-ac1f-74384ab0d808" :answer/id #uuid "4de9d1fa-2114-5200-ac1f-74384ab0d808" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35.5\\pm 1.238" :db/ensure [: